				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-217108#post-1324035</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-217108/scp-889#post-1324035</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 08 Dec 2011 05:55:17 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Gnostalgia</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>322557</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Pretty sure the &quot;there is a direct correlation between the genomic dissimilarity of parents and the lifespan and genetic fitness of offspring&quot; should be &quot;there is an inverse correlation&quot; or &quot;genomic similiarity&quot;.</p> <p>Otherwise that would cause the lab rat x lab rat test to create the least viable offspring, and corn x kitten to be extremely viable.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-217108#post-1322216</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-217108/scp-889#post-1322216</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 06 Dec 2011 19:34:52 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Photosynthetic</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>361873</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Actually, changing it to &quot;The effect of SCP-889 has not been demonstrated to apply to <em>any organisms</em> other than animals or plants.&quot; preserves both exactitude and clarity&#8230;</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-217108#post-1321475</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-217108/scp-889#post-1321475</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 05 Dec 2011 22:39:38 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Lexicality</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>458556</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>To someone completely ignorant of taxonomy (such as myself), &quot;The effect of SCP-889 has not been demonstrated to apply to prokaryotes or eukaryotes other than animals or plants.&quot; doesn't make much sense.<br /> I honestly initially thought it meant &quot;dinosaurs and rocks&quot;, which gave me a moment of &quot;well duh?&quot;<br /> As far as I can work out, that means &quot;This don't work on bacteria or viruses&quot;, which I guess is right from the above comments?<br /> Either way, you might possibly want to sacrifice some exactitude in favour of clarity. :)</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-217108#post-1314426</guid>
